{
  "id": "ss.char.foundress",
  "name": "Foundress",
  "description": "A survivor of the same brood as everything hunting you — same feelers, same organ, same socket in the shell. The organ is `dead`: no halo, no bloom, a hairline crack across cold grey, and that silence is the premise all eight wear in the same place. The comb-cell plating, unchanged — with two shed wing stubs behind it. A queen bites her own wings off when she lands and never flies again, and the scars are the single detail that separates a foundress from any worker in the hive, which is why they are the whole homage here. She wears the hexagon the hive builds with and has no hive: a queen with a brood weapon and nobody to carry it for. Named `foundress` rather than `queen` because `ss.enemy.matriarch` already holds that office, at the other end of it.",
